data: {"type":"response.reasoning_text.done","item_id":"rs_resp_ca4a0de4131046a09ed64e81b1c04fc4","output_index":0,"text":"\nWe need n divisible by 12, exactly 12 divisors, smallest n.\n\nn divisible by 12 = 2^2 · 3. So n = 2^2 · 3 · m.\n\nDivisor count 12: forms: p^11, p^5 q, p^3 q^2, p^2 q r.\n\nSince n has 2^2 and 3^1 as factors, options:\n- p^2 q r form: 2^2 · 3 · q → n = 12q where q prime ≠ 2,3. Smallest q = 5 → n = 60. Check: 60 = 2^2·3·5, divisors = 3·2·2 = 12. Yes.\n- p^3 q^2 form: need 3^2 factor and 2^3: n = 2^3·3^2 = 72, divisors = 4·3=12. 72 > 60.\n- Also 2^2 · 3^2 · ... no, that would be more divisors.\n\nSo smallest is 60.\n\nWait, check n must be divisible by 12: 60/12 = 5 ✓. Divisors of 60: 1,2,3,4,5,6,10,12,15,20,30,60 = 12 ✓.\n\nAnswer: 60.\n","sequence_number":113,"content_index":0}

